  "result": "No, that's not right. A model keeps nothing between conversations, and each call only sees the text you send it.\n\nIt's tempting because a chat app feels continuous. That continuity comes from the app, which resends the earlier messages with every new one. Close the chat and start a new one, and the model has no trace of it.\n\nFor your assistant, you have to build the memory yourself. For example, after a visit you save `{\"student\": \"ana\", \"laser_cutter_trained\": true}` to a file or database. At the start of her next session your code looks up her record and puts it in the prompt. Without that step, the model has never heard of Ana.\n\nDeciding what to save and when to load it is the design question behind your \"what it saves between sessions\" goal. It's a good topic for a lesson if you want one.\n\nDoes that change how you'd plan to store each student's training status?",
